    body: `
<p>English needs the verb "to be" to say where something is: "I am in Hanoi", "The book is on the table". Vietnamese uses one small word instead: <b>ở</b>.</p>
<h3>ở means "be at" and "live at"</h3>
<p><b>ở</b> is a verb of its own. It already means "is at", so it never takes <b>là</b>. With a person, <b>ở</b> can mean both "am in" and "live in". Like every Vietnamese verb, it never changes: the same <b>ở</b> works for I, you, she and they.</p>
{{ex:Tôi ở Hà Nội.|dtohy er? hah_ nohy.|I'm in Hanoi. / I live in Hanoi.}}
{{ex:Chị Lan sống ở Huế.|chee. lahn sohng/ er? hwey/|Lan lives in Hue.}}
<p>In the second sentence <b>ở</b> follows another verb, <b>sống</b> (live), and works like English "in" or "at". It does the same after <b>làm việc</b> (work) and <b>học</b> (study): you work <b>ở</b> a place, you study <b>ở</b> a place.</p>
<h3>Where? X ở đâu?</h3>
<p>English moves "where" to the front. Vietnamese leaves <b>đâu</b> (where) at the end, in the spot where the answer will go. To answer, keep the same frame and put the place where <b>đâu</b> was.</p>
{{ex:Nhà vệ sinh ở đâu?|nyah_ vey. sing er? duhw|Where is the restroom?}}
{{ex:Ngân hàng ở bên cạnh khách sạn.|nguhn hahng_ er? beyn kaing. khaik/ sahn.|The bank is next to the hotel.}}
<h3>On, under, in: the place words</h3>
<p>These words go before the place, just as "on" goes before "the table" in English. Put them right after <b>ở</b>. Two of them also work for time, just as in English: <b>trước</b> is "in front of" or "before", and <b>sau</b> is "behind" or "after". To ask whether someone is somewhere, wrap the sentence in <b>có … không</b>: <b>Chị Lan có ở nhà không?</b> (Is Lan at home?)</p>
<div class="tbl"><table><tr><th>Vietnamese</th><th>English</th></tr><tr><td class="k">trên</td><td>on, above</td></tr><tr><td class="k">dưới</td><td>under, below</td></tr><tr><td class="k">trong</td><td>in, inside</td></tr><tr><td class="k">ngoài</td><td>outside</td></tr><tr><td class="k">bên cạnh</td><td>next to</td></tr><tr><td class="k">trước</td><td>in front of</td></tr><tr><td class="k">sau</td><td>behind</td></tr></table></div>
{{ex:Quyển sách ở trên bàn.|kwee-uhn? saik/ er? cheyn bahn_|The book is on the table.}}
{{ex:Con mèo ở dưới ghế.|kawn mehw_ er? zuu-uhy/ gey/|The cat is under the chair.}}
{{ex:Mẹ tôi ở trong nhà.|meh. dtohy er? chawng nyah_|My mom is inside (the house).}}
<h3>The thing still comes noun first</h3>
<p>The thing you are locating keeps its classifier and its describing words, in the usual order: <b>quyển sách này</b> (this book), <b>con mèo của tôi</b> (my cat). Only then come <b>ở</b> and the place.</p>
{{ex:Con mèo của tôi ở ngoài sân.|kawn mehw_ koo-uh? dtohy er? ngwahy_ suhn|My cat is out in the yard.}}
<div class="tip"><b>Most common mistake:</b> adding <b>là</b> because English says "am" or "is". <b>Tôi là ở Hà Nội</b> → <b>Tôi ở Hà Nội</b>. <b>ở</b> already does the job of "is".</div>
`,
